{"chunk_id":"R1-2505123-001","collection":"ran1_tdoc_chunks","metadata":{"source":["Huawei"],"tdocNumber":"R1-2505123","title":"Reply to LS on power and energy consumption budget for security features in A-IoT"},"point_id":"10275068541207970215"}
and WI on Ambient IoT solutions did not establish a division of power consumption into different aspects and hence RAN WGs have not analyzed which portion of it is left for security functions after non-security related parts are accounted for. In response to the points in the SA3 LS: “Expected operational patterns (e.g., duty cycles, active time slots) of Device Type 1 and the required portion for non-security functions” “Power and energy budgets and constraints during operations” Although RAN1 studied device unavailability (see clause 6.2 of TR 38.769) due to energy harvesting, RAN1 did not break down the power consumption into individual procedures. The above-referenced clause of TR 38.769 includes per-company reports on their assumptions on power and energy budgets for the A-IoT devices, including Device 1. “Any assumptions RAN1 are making regarding security feature support for this device category in terms of power and energy consumption.” RAN1 have made no such assumptions. NOTE: Device 1 has ~1 μW peak power consumption. Further to the aspects contained in the SA3 LS, RAN wishes to remind SA3 that RAN2 made the following agreement relating to AS security. RAN is aware that SA3 also considers NAS security. TSG-RAN advises SA3 that this is the extent of information that can be provided to SA3 from TSG RAN and RAN WGs. RAN expects that completion of the Rel-19 WI in RAN and SA WGs will be as planned. 2. Actions: To SA3: ACTION: SA3 is respectfully requested to take the content of this LS into account. To RAN1: ACTION: RAN guides RAN1 that no additional reply LS to SA3 is needed. 3. Date of Next TSG-RAN Meetings: RAN#109 15-18 September 2025 Beijing, China

